---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Replicate | Fork the Resilience Hub Toolkit for Your Community"
  description="Step-by-step guide to fork, customize, and deploy the Resilience Hub Toolkit for your own community."
>
  <section class="py-16 bg-gradient-to-b from-primary/5 to-background">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-3xl text-center">
      <h1 class="text-hero font-semibold mb-4 text-foreground">
        Replicate This Toolkit
      </h1>
      <p class="text-body-large text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        The Resilience Hub Toolkit is open source and designed to be adapted by other communities.
        Here's how to make it yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="space-y-12">

        <!-- Step 1 -->
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-foreground flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-semibold">1</span>
            <h2 class="text-title font-semibold text-foreground">Fork the repository</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="ml-11 space-y-3">
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Visit <a href="https://github.com/000noyes/resiliencetoolkit.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">github.com/000noyes/resiliencetoolkit.org</a> and click "Fork" to create your own copy.
            </p>
            <pre class="bg-muted rounded-lg p-4 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>git clone https://github.com/YOUR-ORG/resiliencetoolkit.org.git
cd resiliencetoolkit.org/resiliencetoolkit.org
pnpm install
pnpm dev</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 2 -->
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-foreground flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-semibold">2</span>
            <h2 class="text-title font-semibold text-foreground">Edit the content directly</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="ml-11 space-y-3">
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Content lives in <code class="bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">.astro</code> files. No CMS required. Open any page in <code class="bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">src/pages/</code> and edit it directly:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-muted-foreground">
              <li>Replace Vermont-specific references with your region's resources</li>
              <li>Update external links to local emergency management agencies and mutual aid networks</li>
              <li>Edit module titles, phases, and section copy as needed</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Run <code class="bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">pnpm dev</code> to preview changes at <code class="bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">localhost:4321</code>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 3 -->
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-foreground flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-semibold">3</span>
            <h2 class="text-title font-semibold text-foreground">Localize for your region</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="ml-11 space-y-3">
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              The toolkit was built for Vermont, but most content applies anywhere. Key places to localize:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-muted-foreground">
              <li><strong>Knowing Your Community</strong>: Replace the Vermont Town Directory link with your own regional directory</li>
              <li><strong>External links</strong>: Update links to local emergency management agencies, mutual aid networks, and government resources</li>
              <li><strong>Map page</strong>: Point to your region's GIS data or resource map</li>
              <li><strong>Hero copy</strong>: Update the origin story to reference your community's experience</li>
              <li><strong>About page</strong>: Update organization name, contact info, and acknowledgements</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 4 -->
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-foreground flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-semibold">4</span>
            <h2 class="text-title font-semibold text-foreground">Deploy</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="ml-11 space-y-3">
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              The toolkit builds to a static site. No server required. Deploy anywhere:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-muted-foreground">
              <li><strong><a href="https://pages.cloudflare.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Cloudflare Pages</a></strong>: Recommended. Connect your GitHub fork, set build command to <code class="bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">pnpm build</code>, output to <code class="bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">dist</code>. Free tier is generous.</li>
              <li><strong><a href="https://netlify.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Netlify</a></strong>: Git-based deployment, also free</li>
              <li><strong><a href="https://vercel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Vercel</a></strong>: Zero-config deployment</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Build command: <code class="bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">pnpm build</code> &middot;
              Publish directory: <code class="bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">dist</code>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Help -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-2">Need help?</h3>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground">
            We help communities adapt this toolkit. Reach out to
            <a href="mailto:resiliencetoolkit@gocros.org" class="text-primary hover:underline">resiliencetoolkit@gocros.org</a>
            for consultation or technical support.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
